seg-a4c4514276e9 = { "2" }. State what you will score before the run

# text
# c1: run1.events.toml
# c2: receiver-trust
seg-3a3e2be36c65 = The events file gives the intervals the scenario defines. Copy <c1/> into a <c2/> scenario, add any prediction you want checked, and fix the monitor thresholds and tolerances <b>before</b> the receiver runs. Do not adjust them after seeing the log; the scenario, the thresholds and the log's SHA-256 are all in the result's hash.

# text
# c1: jamming
# c2: jamming
# c3: other
# c4: kind
seg-d07b9ad8cfa9 = The exported events carry the scenario's own kind: a <c1/> scenario's jammer is <c2/>; a navigation-state outage is <c3/>, because the scenario states that GNSS was unavailable, not how. Change the <c4/> to match what you configure the simulator to do.

